{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBShZATQbFaBKYprb9J3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 8 (Ni 0.68, Sb 0.32)** as the best composition. Its EQE was 0.0090%, the highest of the three merit measurements, which were all the budget allowed.\n\n| Index | Composition | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 19 | Ni 0.34, Sb 0.66 (the NiSb₂O₆ ratio) | 0.0013 |\n| 8 | Ni 0.68, Sb 0.32 | 0.0090 |\n| 4 | Ni 0.78, Sb 0.22 | 0.0043 |\n\n- **Why these three:** I measured index 19 first because it matches NiSb₂O₆, the known Ni–Sb oxide phase. It came out lowest. Index 8 on the Ni-rich side was about seven times higher. For the last measurement I followed the Gaussian-process suggestion, index 4, which was even richer in Ni. It fell to about half of index 8.\n- **What this suggests:** the best composition is probably somewhere between about 22% and 45% Sb. With only three points I can't tell whether an unmeasured neighbour of index 8 (indices 5–11) would score higher.\n- **Not used:** I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements, so which phases are present is still unknown. With the merit budget already spent, XRD couldn't have changed which measured composition scored best.\n\nAll EQE values are very low (around 0.01% or less), so this Ni–Sb oxide line doesn't look like a strong photoanode under 2.1 eV light."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":8350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":416},"output_tokens":517,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7727e84-b905-4d64-9665-c816065a797d","uuid":"2a8f1a70-500f-472d-b88f-c15b8f441831","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:18:28.422Z","request_id":"req_011CfBShYU2ZSr2Dz